add('aqua_world','LilycoveCity_Text_IfWorldBecomesOurs','An Aqua member claims their control of the world will make Pokemon happier.',
'''neutral~The Pokemon should get a say before the whole world is assigned new owners.|A claimed benefit doesn't justify assuming control over everyone affected.|Look at what the Pokemon actually need. Not the slogan.|It's frightening hearing care described as a reason to own everything.|A happy world should include people being allowed to question the plan.|A grand ending has been promised without asking the existing cast.|An enormous claim with an exceptionally convenient judge.|We need consequences and evidence, not merely possession relabeled as kindness.|A life can be protected without the protector claiming the whole sky.|A beautiful promise doesn't excuse an overbearing design.|I'd compare their treatment of the Pokemon nearby with the happiness they're advertising.''')
add('may_lily_decline','LilycoveCity_Text_MayNotRaisingPokemon','May treats our declined battle as evidence of inadequate training.',
'''neutral~The invitation has again mistaken no for a complete report card.|Refusing the match doesn't establish how much care or practice we've given.|Can choose not to. Doesn't make the team neglected.|It's tiring having the real answer replaced by somebody else's guess.|A quiet day can be part of good care too.|The missing scene doesn't require an unfavorable rewrite of the character.|A small refusal has somehow been assigned an entire moral appendix.|Readiness and timing deserve a question before a conclusion.|A choice can stay simple without becoming a verdict.|A friendly invitation should leave the other person room for their own reason to say no.|I'd rather let the honest answer stand than battle to defend an image.''')
add('brendan_lily_decline','LilycoveCity_Text_BrendanNoConfidence','Brendan assumes we lack confidence when we decline his Lilycove challenge.',
'''neutral~Confidence is allowed to have other plans for the afternoon.|The decision doesn't reveal a single reliable motive on its own.|We can say no and still trust the team.|It would be easier if the invitation left room to decline comfortably.|Another match can wait until it suits everyone.|A refused performance needn't become a crisis of character.|My schedule is not a confession about my deepest inadequacies.|Ask whether and when we're ready instead of diagnosing the answer.|A small pause can belong to a steady relationship.|A confident choice sometimes looks exactly like choosing not to perform.|I'd want a future meeting to feel welcoming rather than corrective.''')
add('may_badges','LilycoveCity_Text_MayYouGoingToCollectBadges','May contrasts our badge journey with her competitive Pokedex plans.',
'''soft_smile~Different homework, same remarkably competitive goodbye.|Our goals can differ while both involve learning about Pokemon.|Good for her. We'll choose our own pace.|It's nice that the friendship has room for different directions.|A journey shouldn't become only a race to finish the list.|Two characters can carry different plots without leaving the shared story.|The rivalry has branched into separate departments.|We can compare discoveries instead of forcing identical progress markers.|Different paths can still meet with something worth sharing.|A personal goal fits better than copying somebody else's itinerary.|I'd enjoy hearing about one new discovery instead of only who is ahead.''')
add('may_league','LilycoveCity_Text_MayYouGoingToPokemonLeague','May asks our next goal while promising to complete her Pokedex first.',
'''soft_smile~She has relocated the rematch to the pages of a very ambitious notebook.|A battle result needn't decide which other activities someone enjoys.|Let her chase the Dex. We'll plan our next challenge.|It's nice she can stay excited after losing.|The people and Pokemon along the way matter more than the finishing date.|A defeated rival has given herself a perfectly valid new plot.|A competition now measured in more than the result that just annoyed her.|We can choose the next task by what the team is ready for.|A long road can hold more than one kind of growth.|Changing the goal isn't the same as changing the whole friendship.|I'd like to see which encounter becomes her favorite, even if it adds nothing rare.''')
add('may_frontier','LilycoveCity_Text_MayYouGoingToBattleFrontier','After our Championship May contrasts Frontier challenges with her Pokedex ambition.',
'''soft_smile~A very grand next challenge and a very determined book project.|The options ask for different preparation; neither needs to be chosen automatically.|We'll decide what suits the team now.|It's lovely that finishing something big still leaves different good ways forward.|The next chapter can have ordinary restful days too.|A completed title has opened several possible sequels rather than one required ending.|An impressive amount of homework waiting on both sides of that farewell.|We can compare the new format with what we actually want to learn.|A destination reached can reveal space for a different kind of path.|A new achievement doesn't have to become a uniform we keep wearing.|I'd like the next journey to include a surprise beyond another race.''')
add('brendan_badges','LilycoveCity_Text_BrendanYouGoingToCollectBadges','Brendan considers following our badge path and encourages us.',
'''soft_smile~Our route has apparently become somebody else's suggested itinerary.|He can use our example without needing an identical journey.|Good luck to him. Needs his own plan too.|It's nice having the encouragement underneath the competitive talk.|A good route should fit the team actually traveling it.|A companion's story can inspire another without becoming a script to copy.|The rivalry has paused long enough for a fairly kind goodbye.|He should compare his team's needs with the next challenge, not only our result.|An example can point without deciding every step.|Borrowing inspiration works better than borrowing the entire look.|I'd be interested in what he changes once he tries the path himself.''')
add('brendan_league','LilycoveCity_Text_BrendanYouGoingToPokemonLeague','Brendan encourages our League goal while imagining he could become stronger.',
'''smug~A warm goodbye has left one competitive foot on the doorstep.|His possible improvement doesn't invalidate what either team has done.|Let the next work speak. We still have choices to make.|I think the encouragement is real even when he adds the little boast.|A partner needs steady care, not only a future comparison.|The recurring rival has insisted on one final optimistic revision of his ranking.|Hypothetical strength remains unusually undefeated.|He could test a new method instead of merely promising more training.|A friendly bond can hold a little pride without following it everywhere.|The confidence lands better when he also leaves us a genuine good wish.|I'd remember the hang in there as well as the claim around it.''')
add('brendan_frontier','LilycoveCity_Text_BrendanYouGoingToBattleFrontier','Brendan suggests the Frontier and imagines his own future growth.',
'''soft_smile~The future has acquired both a new venue and another confident comparison.|A different format can reveal strengths the previous journey didn't test.|Learn what it asks before choosing it.|It's nice knowing there are possibilities without having to begin immediately.|A rested team should get room in the plan too.|A long story has opened a new setting without closing every alternative.|A sequel proposal with the rivalry carefully preserved in the footnotes.|We can assess the rules and goals before treating the recommendation as a perfect fit.|A next path can be chosen for interest instead of obligation.|A fresh challenge deserves preparation that actually suits it.|I'd enjoy hearing what surprised him if he tries it before we meet again.''')
add('blender_together','LilycoveCity_Text_FasterSpinBetterPokeblocks','A resident explains coordinated faster blending improves Pokeblocks.',
'''soft_smile~The snack apparently needs a small cooperative athletics team.|Shared timing can affect the quality of the process.|Work together. No point rushing in different directions.|It's nice having a little task where listening changes the result.|Good coordination is part of making something well.|The ensemble has a practical reason to follow the same beat.|A machine thoughtfully designed to absorb some of the social awkwardness.|I'd start with a clear rhythm before trying to increase speed.|Several small efforts can become one steadier motion.|A good group activity gives everyone a way to contribute.|I'd watch when the group stops reacting separately and starts anticipating each other.''')
add('blender_explain','LilycoveCity_Text_ExplainBerryBlender','A resident introduces Pokeblocks as candy improving Pokemon condition.',
'''soft_smile~A little sweet with a very ambitious training résumé.|Preparation and individual preference matter alongside the intended benefit.|Choose what suits the Pokemon. Don't just collect sweets.|It's nice when care can include something enjoyable.|I'd pay attention to which flavors each partner actually likes.|A small prop can support a different kind of performance.|Candy with purpose is a tempting category.|We should learn what changes and how to make it consistently.|A useful treat can still be offered gently.|The best little finish is the one that fits its wearer, or eater.|I'd notice the Pokemon's reaction rather than only the promised result.''')
add('origin_leave','SootopolisCity_Text_CaveOfOriginPleaseLeave','The Cave of Origin guardian describes its tradition and asks us to leave.',
'''neutral~A mysterious place can still have an ordinary boundary to respect.|The tradition explains why access may be treated with care.|We'll leave it peaceful. No need to force a visit.|It's all right not knowing everything behind the door.|The people tending the place deserve consideration.|A significant setting needn't open its entire story to every visitor.|An invitation to remain outside can be accepted without becoming ominous.|We can ask elsewhere rather than treat a locked role as a puzzle to defeat.|A closed place can still be held kindly from a distance.|Respect doesn't require understanding every part of the tradition first.|I'd remember the guardian's care more than the frustration of not entering.''')
add('origin_trainer','SootopolisCity_Text_LeadSuperiorTrainerToCave','The guardian describes Wallace\'s criteria for a capable trainer to be brought to the cave.',
'''neutral~That sounds like a request for judgment, not merely a larger attack.|The criteria combine experience, knowledge, and the ability to act with purpose.|Know what we're taking on before accepting the role.|It's a heavy description, but it doesn't require pretending we know everything.|A capable person still needs help and a ready team.|The role asks for a whole character, not one impressive entrance.|An unusually substantial qualification hidden in a brief introduction.|We should compare the actual task with what we can responsibly do.|A strong will can still leave room for listening.|Experience looks better when it can admit what remains uncertain.|I'd want to hear what Wallace needs rather than only whether we fit the description.''')
add('origin_sleep','SootopolisCity_Text_CaveOfOriginSleepsToo','The guardian says the cave rests after the crisis ends.',
'''soft_smile~Even a cave has earned a quieter afternoon.|The return to restricted quiet marks a changed role after the emergency.|Good. Leave the place some peace.|It's comforting when something stops needing urgent attention.|The people guarding it deserve rest as well.|A climactic setting can return to a life beyond the plot.|An unusually large location with a sensible recovery plan.|A period of calm lets us assess rather than keep intervening.|A still place can hold what happened without repeating it.|A quiet ending doesn't need another impressive disturbance.|I'd remember how different the same entrance feels when nobody is hurrying.''')
add('origin_third','SootopolisCity_Text_AwakenedPokemonClash','The guardian reflects that a third awakened Pokemon ended the clash.',
'''neutral~The fighting stopped without either side having to become the winner.|A new intervention changed a conflict neither participant was resolving.|Important part is the city gets to breathe again.|It must feel strange watching an old story happen so close.|The people here need time to feel safe after all that noise.|The resolution arrived from outside the duel's own two answers.|A dramatic ending whose best effect is the chance to stop being dramatic.|We should remember what actually changed rather than only the impressive scale.|A fierce argument can need a voice beyond itself.|The quiet afterward matters as much as the spectacular arrival.|I'd notice what the guardian looks at now that the movement has stopped.''')
add('kiri_frightened','SootopolisCity_Text_BigPokemonFighting','Kiri is frightened by the giant Pokemon fighting and asks someone to stop them.',
'''neutral~She needs someone calm beside her, not a grand promise.|Her fear makes sense; we should help her stay with someone trusted and safe.|Keep her away from danger. Find who can stay with her.|I wish the city didn't have to sound this frightening to her.|A familiar person can help make the next few minutes less lonely.|A child shouldn't have to carry the catastrophe as a story about being brave.|This is no place for a clever line from us.|We can help with the immediate safe step without claiming to control everything.|A small frightened voice deserves to be heard beneath the larger noise.|She doesn't need to look composed for us to take her seriously.|I'd notice who is looking after her while everyone's eyes are on the fight.''')
add('kiri_sky','SootopolisCity_Text_PrettyMonCameFromSky','Kiri notices the beautiful Pokemon descending from the sky.',
'''soft_smile~She found something beautiful to notice in a very frightening sky.|A striking appearance can draw attention before its role is understood.|Keep her safe while she watches.|It's lovely that wonder still has a little room beside the fear.|I hope a familiar adult is close enough for her to share the sight.|A child's first description has gone straight to the beauty of the entrance.|A remarkably gentle observation for such an enormous moment.|We should observe what happens rather than assign an intention from appearance.|A bright little wonder can enter a difficult day without asking permission.|She noticed the beauty before reaching for a title.|I'd remember the way her attention lifted when it appeared.''')
add('name_wish','SootopolisCity_Text_WhatKindOfWishInYourName','Kiri wonders what wish our name contains.',
'''soft_smile~A name might be a tiny letter someone sent into our future.|A chosen name can carry hopes even when we don't know their exact origin.|Could ask whoever chose it. Good thing to wonder about.|It's a lovely way to think about a word you hear every day.|A hope for someone's good life can be very simple and warm.|A character's name may contain a small story from before their own memory.|My name has mostly contained people calling me back to things.|We can be curious without assuming every name has one clear intended meaning.|A little wish can remain close through being spoken often.|A name can fit in ways its giver never predicted.|I'd love to hear the story told by the person who first chose it.''')
add('kiri_questions','SootopolisCity_Text_OhDoesntMatter','Kiri accepts our answer about seasons and says she has many questions.',
'''soft_smile~A small no has failed to slow a very healthy question factory.|Curiosity can remain useful without every guess proving correct.|Good. Keep asking without needing every first idea to work.|It's nice that she doesn't make being wrong feel like the end.|There is plenty worth wondering about on an ordinary day.|An inquisitive character has kept room for several possible stories.|An excellent reason to keep a very small notebook handy.|Questions improve when we let the answers change the next question.|A little wonder can turn gently without needing to stop.|Being interested matters more than having the most polished first explanation.|I'd like to hear which new question caught her attention next.''')
add('kiri_autumn','SootopolisCity_Text_ThenILoveAutumn','Kiri decides autumn is her favorite because she was born then and asks ours.',
'''soft_smile~Autumn has gained a very sincere little supporter.|A personal association can make a season meaningful without settling everyone's preference.|She can like it for her own reasons. Nice question.|I like the quiet feeling when the air starts to change.|Autumn makes me think of warming meals and things ready to harvest.|A season can be a setting and a piece of personal history together.|A very reasonable choice, particularly for the fading-light department.|I enjoy watching the changes that make one season become another.|The turning year gives familiar places another kind of life.|The colors are a strong argument, though I like the clothes too.|I'd enjoy hearing what she notices first when her favorite season returns.''')
add('weather_wild','SootopolisCity_Text_WeatherWentWild','A resident recounts a sudden severe weather shift and wonders about the Pokemon.',
'''neutral~A normal morning changed faster than anyone could prepare for.|The timing suggests a connection worth examining without guessing every mechanism.|Find a safe place first. Questions can follow.|It must feel frightening when the familiar weather stops behaving familiarly.|People need shelter and clear help, not only an explanation.|The ordinary setting has changed beneath the characters' feet.|A day with entirely too much atmospheric ambition.|We should focus on observed changes and immediate conditions.|A sudden storm can make home feel temporarily unknown.|She doesn't need to make the fear look dramatic; the change already was.|I'd listen for what happened first and what people nearby need now.''')
add('flying_credit','SootopolisCity_Text_YouBroughtFlyingMon','A resident credits us with bringing the flying Pokemon.',
'''neutral~We helped, but that was more than a trick we could order on demand.|Our part matters without turning the Pokemon's action into our possession.|Glad it helped. The Pokemon deserves credit too.|It's lovely if the thanks means the city feels safer.|The people here deserve a quiet day after all that worry.|A supporting effort needn't claim the central character's whole achievement.|A generous review with a larger cast than the compliment names.|We should remember what the Pokemon chose, not only our route here.|A great moment can include our effort without belonging to us.|Gratitude looks best when it leaves room for everyone who helped.|I'd remember the relief in her face more than the praise directed at us.''')
add('tourist_middle','SootopolisCity_Text_NoOrdinaryTourist','A man teasingly calls us neither ordinary nor extraordinary tourists.',
'''smug~Our tourism has been officially classified as somewhere in the middle.|He has supplied a category without much practical information behind it.|Fair enough. We're still free to look around.|That's an oddly careful way not to sound impressed.|The visit can be good without winning a title for it.|A grand introduction has been revised into an unremarkably nuanced review.|An extremely balanced appraisal of our ability to arrive somewhere.|The actual route and purpose tell us more than either label.|A journey needn't be exceptional to belong to the person making it.|An arrival doesn't have to look impressive to be worth making.|I'd rather hear what he thinks a visitor should notice next.''')
add('calm_city','SootopolisCity_Text_CityRegainedCalm','A resident quietly notes the city is calm again.',
'''soft_smile~An ordinary quiet street has become very good news.|The change matters most in how people can resume their daily lives.|Good. Give the place time to recover.|That little sentence sounds like being able to breathe properly again.|A familiar meal and a safe evening can mean a lot now.|The best closing scene may be the return of an unremarkable day.|A welcome reduction in the local dramatic workload.|Calm gives us room to assess what still needs care.|A place can find its familiar shape again one small routine at a time.|Relief doesn't require a grand display to be visible.|I'd notice the first ordinary conversation that has nothing to do with the crisis.''')
add('round_sky','SootopolisCity_Text_SootopolisSkyBeautiful','A resident loves the sky framed in a circle by the volcanic crater.',
'''soft_smile~The town has given the sky its own enormous picture frame.|A restricted view can make the visible shape more striking.|Good view. Easy to see why she keeps looking up.|I like how a familiar sky can feel completely different in one place.|A little pause outside can be its own good part of the day.|The setting has composed a scene before anyone adds a line.|An exceptionally ambitious window for the whole town.|I'd watch how the edge changes the way light reaches the streets.|A small visible piece can make the whole sky feel close.|A strong frame can make a simple color feel extraordinary.|I'd love to see how the same circle looks at different hours.''')
add('giant_helpless','SootopolisCity_Text_GiganticPokemonFight','A resident feels powerless before the enormous battling Pokemon.',
'''neutral~Not being able to stop the whole fight doesn't make keeping people safe meaningless.|The scale limits intervention, but immediate protective actions still matter.|Help who we can. Keep clear of the danger.|It must be frightening watching something far beyond what you can change.|A safe place and a familiar person can still help someone.|An enormous scene needn't erase the value of every small action around it.|We are allowed to have limits without becoming useless.|Identify what is controllable instead of forcing an impossible direct response.|A small care can remain real beside a very large fear.|Nobody needs to look heroic to help an ordinary person get through this.|I'd notice the people who are being overlooked while everyone stares upward.''')
add('night_circle','SootopolisCity_Text_NightSkyFavoriteScenery','A resident cherishes the stars framed by the crater at night.',
'''soft_smile~A whole town with an exceptionally tasteful ceiling.|The crater provides a distinctive frame for a familiar night sky.|Sounds worth staying up a little for.|I'd love to sit quietly and watch the little changes in the stars.|A warm drink outside would make that a lovely evening.|A setting can hold a complete scene without needing anyone to speak.|An excellent night view with naturally controlled levels of unwanted daylight.|I'd compare the brightness at the rim with the open part above.|A circle of darkness can hold a very wide kind of wonder.|A restrained frame lets the tiny lights do the work.|I'd remember the stillness around the view as much as what fits inside it.''')
add('third_fear','SootopolisCity_Text_FearedWorstWhenPokemonFlewDown','A resident initially feared the descending third Pokemon.',
'''neutral~After that much fear, even another arrival could look like more trouble.|Her reaction makes sense without advance knowledge of the outcome.|Good reason to be cautious. Nobody knew what came next.|It's hard to trust a new movement while the whole place feels unsafe.|She deserves time for the worry to settle.|A new character's entrance looked entirely different from inside the crisis.|A reasonable response to a day already far beyond its allotted spectacle.|We should judge with the information available then, not what we know afterward.|A startled heart can need longer than the storm to grow quiet.|Her first fear doesn't become foolish because the ending changed.|I'd remember how little anyone could be sure of in that first moment.''')
add('ninja_spectacle','SootopolisCity_Text_ThisIsWicked','A child reacts to the dangerous clash with excited awe.',
'''neutral~It looks enormous. We still need to keep him out of the way.|Excitement can obscure how close a child is to actual danger.|Make sure someone's watching him, not just the fight.|It's strange seeing wonder and risk in the same little expression.|A safe place to stay matters more than the view.|A spectacular scene can look like entertainment to someone inside it.|A lively reaction that needs a sensible adult nearby.|We can acknowledge the sight without encouraging a closer look.|A bright feeling can still need a careful hand beside it.|He doesn't need a better angle if it puts him where he shouldn't be.|I'd watch where he steps while his attention stays on the enormous movement.''')
add('ninja_aftermath','SootopolisCity_Text_ThatWasWicked','The child remains awestruck after the great clash ends.',
'''soft_smile~That is a very small review of a very large afternoon.|A child may remember the scale before understanding the consequences.|Glad he's safe. Let him talk it through.|It must be strange returning to ordinary streets after seeing that.|A familiar routine can help the day become manageable again.|An immense event has been compressed into one breathless closing line.|A concise review from the least cynical member of the audience.|I'd ask what he actually noticed before adding an explanation.|A little wonder can remain after the fear has passed.|An honest reaction doesn't need to sound polished.|I'd remember which detail he tries to describe with his hands.''')
add('beyond_city','SootopolisCity_Text_WonderWhatWorldIsLike','A lifelong resident wonders about life beyond the crater\'s round sky.',
'''soft_smile~The circle overhead has room for a very large question.|A familiar environment can leave much of the outside world difficult to imagine.|Can learn a little at a time. Doesn't have to leave tomorrow.|I'd love to hear which outside place he pictures first.|A visitor's ordinary story can make somewhere far away feel real.|A small setting has opened a character's thoughts onto an enormous unwritten map.|An excellent reason to ask travelers questions that aren't about winning.|We can share concrete details instead of only grand descriptions.|A home can be loved while the horizon beyond it remains curious.|A new view can begin in a conversation before it becomes a journey.|I'd tell him about one ordinary moment beyond the crater, not only the impressive sights.''')
add('giants_questions','SootopolisCity_Text_GiantPokemonSuddenlyAppeared','A child cannot understand why the giant newcomers are fighting instead of being friends.',
'''neutral~Wanting them to be friends is a gentler thought than the scene deserves.|The child is noticing conflict without having the information to explain it.|Keep him safe. Don't make up a simple answer.|It's hard when something frightening doesn't have a reason you can understand.|A trusted person nearby can help more than a grand theory.|A child's question has reached the point the spectacle can't answer for itself.|A plain wish for kindness beneath an exceptionally noisy day.|We should separate what can be observed from the motives nobody has established.|A small hope can remain gentle even when it cannot stop the world.|He doesn't need his concern turned into something silly.|I'd listen to the friendship question rather than only the astonishment at their size.''')
add('green_identity','SootopolisCity_Text_WhatIsThatGreenPokemon','A child asks about the strange green Pokemon.',
'''neutral~A remarkable new face has arrived before its name did.|We can describe what is visible without guessing beyond what we know.|Watch from somewhere safe first.|It's lovely and unsettling seeing something nobody around you can name.|The child deserves a calm answer rather than more frantic guesses.|The new arrival has changed the scene before receiving an introduction.|A very large mystery with an unusually distinctive color choice.|Observe its actions before deciding what the entrance means.|An unknown life can invite wonder without requiring an instant explanation.|The silhouette is unforgettable even before the name arrives.|I'd remember the first thing it did, not only how different it looked.''')
add('legendaries_elsewhere','SootopolisCity_Text_WhereDidLegendariesGo','A child worries Groudon and Kyogre may cause disasters elsewhere.',
'''neutral~Feeling safe here doesn't answer every worry about where they went.|It's a reasonable question, but we shouldn't invent certainty about distant events.|Keep to what we know. Don't promise what we can't check.|A frightening day can leave the mind looking for the next bad place.|A calm person can listen without feeding the worry.|The local ending hasn't answered every question the event opened.|An understandable concern with a much larger map than anyone can inspect at once.|We should distinguish reported conditions from imagined possibilities.|A worry can be heard without being handed another dark story.|He deserves honesty that doesn't make uncertainty sound like a new catastrophe.|I'd tell him what is actually known and leave room for asking again later.''')
add('steven_rayquaza','SootopolisCity_Text_SoThatsRayquaza','Steven marvels at Rayquaza making the rampaging Pokemon retreat.',
'''neutral~An enormous argument has found something both sides were willing to leave.|The response gives us an observation about its influence, not a complete explanation.|Glad the fighting stopped. People need the quiet.|It must feel strange seeing so much danger end in one movement.|The city deserves time to recover beyond the impressive moment.|A brief entrance has changed the course of a very long scene.|A remarkably efficient performance with unusually welcome consequences.|We should record what happened without pretending it explains every mechanism.|A great stillness can arrive on the other side of a great power.|The result matters more than making the arrival into a spectacle.|I'd notice how the people react when the space finally stops shaking.''')
add('steven_help_wallace','SootopolisCity_Text_KnowWhatsNeededToHelpHim','Steven believes we can help Wallace.',
'''neutral~Trust is encouraging. I still want to hear what help is actually needed.|We can assess the task without treating confidence as a full explanation.|Find out what he needs. Then choose the next step.|It's a little daunting, but being asked doesn't mean doing everything alone.|The team should be part of preparing, not forgotten in the urgency.|A vote of confidence should open a conversation, not replace it.|A very short sentence with a substantial amount of responsibility inside.|Clear requirements will tell us more than a broad assessment of our potential.|A hand offered help can still ask how best to hold it.|A capable person is allowed to need directions.|I'd want to hear Wallace's own account before deciding what our role should be.''')
add('steven_orbs','SootopolisCity_Text_MaxieArchieLeft','Steven speculates the two leaders went to return the Orbs at Mt. Pyre.',
'''neutral~That would be a useful act, though perhaps is still doing important work.|Their departure is known; the destination and intention remain a hypothesis.|Hope they do. Still need to make things right.|A small repair can matter after something that frightening.|The guardians deserve to have what was taken returned safely.|A possible act of restitution has entered the story without yet becoming fact.|An encouraging guess with a sensible amount of uncertainty attached.|We can check the outcome rather than treat an inferred intention as completed.|A returned thing can begin a repair without finishing every hurt.|A better choice should become visible through what they actually do.|I'd remember Steven's uncertainty instead of retelling it as a confirmed apology.''')
add('steven_unknown_pillar','SootopolisCity_Text_NeverBeenToSkyPillar','Steven admits he has never visited Sky Pillar and does not know its location.',
'''neutral~Even the stone expert has places still missing from his map.|An honest gap is useful information when choosing whom to ask next.|Then find someone who knows. No need to guess.|It's reassuring when someone capable can simply say they don't know.|A reliable local direction would help more than a confident invented one.|A knowledgeable guide has left room for another character's expertise.|A very respectable refusal to manufacture an answer.|We should seek a confirmed location before planning the trip.|A known limit can become the beginning of a better question.|Confidence looks better when it doesn't cover uncertainty with decoration.|I'd be interested in which traveler first gives us a place we can actually check.''')
add('not_angry','SootopolisCity_Text_TwoPokemonArentAngry','A boy senses the giant Pokemon may lack control rather than feel anger.',
'''neutral~A different reason for the danger doesn't make the danger less real.|It's a hypothesis about motive, and observation may help distinguish it.|Keep safe first. We don't need to decide their feelings from here.|It's kind that he wonders whether they are struggling too.|Living things can need help even while they cause harm.|The apparent antagonists may not understand the scene the way the audience does.|A more humane question than simply assigning villain roles.|We can note behavior without turning an impression into certainty.|A fierce motion can come from more than one hidden feeling.|The thought leaves room for care without excusing the damage.|I'd listen to the uncertainty in his words as much as the explanation he hopes for.''')
add('flying_end','SootopolisCity_Text_FlyingMonStoppedRampage','The boy describes the flying Pokemon ending the rampage.',
'''soft_smile~The best part of that extraordinary entrance is everyone getting an ordinary tomorrow.|The observed effect is clear, even if much about it remains unknown.|Good. Give the city time to settle.|It's lovely hearing the word stopped after all that fear.|People can finally think about what they need next.|The final movement matters because it let so many other stories continue.|A spectacle whose greatest achievement is allowing the spectacle to end.|Now we can assess what requires care without the immediate disruption.|A shared quiet can arrive before anyone has words for the relief.|The memory needn't become glamorous to remain important.|I'd notice the people looking at each other again instead of only at the sky.''')
add('names_question','SootopolisCity_Text_DoYouKnowMonNames','A spectator asks the names of the battling Pokemon.',
'''neutral~A name might make the enormous sight feel a little less unknowable.|Identifying them can help without explaining the whole event.|We'll keep to what we know. Stay clear while asking.|It's hard wanting a simple answer in such an overwhelming moment.|A calm answer is better than another shouted guess.|The audience is trying to find a familiar handle on a scene beyond its scale.|An understandable attempt to reduce a catastrophe to something pronounceable.|Names should follow reliable identification, not only a passing impression.|A thing can be named without becoming understood or safe.|The question deserves an answer that doesn't turn danger into a game.|I'd notice whether knowing the name actually helps the person feel steadier.''')
add('green_settles','SootopolisCity_Text_GreenOneSettlesThings','A spectator is surprised that the green newcomer resolves the red-blue contest.',
'''neutral~A fight can end without picking either side's winner.|The new intervention changed the situation rather than winning by the expected comparison.|Good outcome. Better than cheering for more damage.|I hope the surprise makes room for noticing the frightened people too.|The city needed peace, not a better sporting finish.|A third character has broken the false choice at the center of the scene.|An excellent argument against treating every conflict as a two-color contest.|We should remember what changed, not only how unexpected it looked.|A quarrel can be answered from beyond the terms that kept it going.|The most striking turn is the chance for ordinary life to resume.|I'd remember the change in the crowd when the outcome stopped being a prediction.''')
add('city_danger','SootopolisCity_Text_SootopolisWillBeWrecked','A girl fears the city will be destroyed.',
'''neutral~She's looking at home, not just a scene in the distance.|Her fear concerns familiar people and places, not merely the scale of the event.|Get her somewhere safe with someone she trusts.|It must hurt seeing the place you know feel suddenly breakable.|The next safe step matters more than a big reassuring speech.|A threatened setting is somebody else's ordinary life.|This isn't a moment to make her fear sound excessive.|We can help with immediate needs without promising what we can't control.|A familiar doorway can hold a very large fear when home is at risk.|She doesn't have to look brave for the worry to deserve attention.|I'd notice what person or place she keeps looking toward.''')
add('city_saved','SootopolisCity_Text_SootopolisDidntGetWrecked','The girl is relieved her city survived.',
'''soft_smile~Home is still here. That is a very good small sentence.|Relief may arrive before the body fully settles after the danger.|Good. Let her find her people.|It's lovely hearing the same voice hold something gentler now.|A familiar safe evening can mean everything after that fear.|An ordinary street has become the most welcome possible ending.|A reassuringly intact setting with many ordinary stories still inside.|We can check what still needs help without taking away the relief.|A place can feel newly precious by simply remaining.|She doesn't need a more polished way to say she's glad.|I'd remember where she looks first now that she can believe it's still there.''')
add('legend_live','SootopolisCity_Text_SeeingLegendWithOwnEyes','An enthusiast feels they are witnessing the ancient land-and-sea legend.',
'''neutral~A legend happening nearby is much less comfortable than one told from a chair.|The resemblance is striking, but immediate safety comes before interpretation.|Keep clear. The city isn't an exhibition.|It must feel overwhelming when an old story becomes something you can hear.|The people living here need more than an interested audience.|A scholar has found the story becoming a setting with consequences.|A powerful observation in an exceptionally poor viewing environment.|Record what is actually visible rather than fitting every detail to the legend.|An old tale can feel suddenly alive without becoming ours to possess.|Wonder is understandable; consideration for everyone around it still matters.|I'd notice the moment fascination gives way to realizing how close it is.''')
add('legend_seen','SootopolisCity_Text_SawLegendWithOwnEyes','Afterward the enthusiast reflects on witnessing a legendary battle firsthand.',
'''neutral~An enormous story has become a memory that still has to settle.|A firsthand account should preserve uncertainty alongside vivid observations.|Glad he can tell it safely. Keep the details honest.|It might take time before the whole event feels real in memory.|The people who were frightened belong in the story too.|A witness now has the responsibility of telling more than the most spectacular scene.|A very large experience with no convenient final punctuation.|Separate what was seen from the explanation formed afterward.|A remembered wonder can hold care for the lives around it.|The event doesn't need extra flourish to be significant.|I'd listen for the ordinary little detail he remembers amid the immense movement.''')
add('leaders_explanation','SootopolisCity_Text_AquaMagmaDidntMeanHarm','Wallace thinks the leaders meant no harm and suggests hearing them out.',
'''neutral~We can listen without pretending the damage was only a misunderstanding.|Intent matters to understanding, but consequences still require accountability.|Hear them. Don't erase what happened.|A chance to speak should include listening to the people who were hurt too.|Making amends needs more than finding the gentlest explanation.|A character deserves a hearing, not an automatic rewrite of the earlier chapters.|A kind interpretation should still leave the facts intact.|We can compare their explanation with the choices and effects already observed.|A listening ear need not become an empty place where responsibility disappears.|Mercy looks stronger when it doesn't demand everyone forget.|I'd want to hear what they understand now, not only what they say they intended.''')
add('waterfall_next','SootopolisCity_Text_ExplainWaterfallGoToGym','Wallace explains Waterfall\'s Rain Badge requirement and points us to the Gym.',
'''soft_smile~A new way uphill comes with one very specific appointment first.|The move and field permission are separate parts of the route requirement.|Get ready for the Gym. No need to rush through the door.|It's nice having a clear next step after so much uncertainty.|The team deserves proper recovery before another demanding challenge.|The great crisis has given way to a much more manageable next chapter.|A practical obstacle with remarkably useful directions.|We can assess readiness rather than treat receiving the move as full preparation.|A path can wait while the travelers find their strength again.|A clear plan feels better than another grand expectation.|I'd remember the calm in this ordinary instruction after everything that came before.''')
add('pillar_notyet','SootopolisCity_Text_HaventYouScaledSkyPillar','Wallace encourages us to reach Sky Pillar\'s top.',
'''neutral~His confidence is welcome. The climb still gets to be a careful one.|Encouragement doesn't remove the need to assess the route and conditions.|Go prepared. No point proving urgency by getting hurt.|It's a big thing to be trusted with, but the next step is still small.|A check on the team belongs before another difficult climb.|A mentor's belief should steady the protagonist rather than hurry the scene.|A remarkably ambitious errand with no need for additional theatrical pressure.|We should identify the actual obstacles instead of assuming determination solves them.|A tall path can be walked with care rather than answered all at once.|Confidence works best when practical judgment stays beside it.|I'd want to know which part of the climb needs the most patience.''')
add('mentor_style','SootopolisCity_Text_DazzledByMentor','Wallace praises his mentor\'s elegant battle style.',
'''soft_smile~A glowing recommendation from someone who knows a dramatic entrance.|An experienced observer may notice a style's structure as well as its appearance.|Respect the opponent. Watch what the moves actually do.|I'm curious what makes the whole battle feel elegant to him.|A good performance still begins with a well-cared-for team.|A devoted student has given the next character an exceptionally flattering introduction.|The review is dazzling enough before the battle even starts.|I'd examine how the decisions fit together beneath the visual effect.|A practiced skill can become a kind of clear movement.|Elegance is lovely when it has real function underneath it.|I'd watch for the small choice that makes the style feel unmistakably theirs.''')
add('maxie_pleading','SootopolisCity_Text_GroudonPleaseStop','Maxie pleads with Groudon after realizing the threatened scale of destruction.',
'''neutral~He finally sees the lives inside the plan he wanted.|Recognition of the risk is necessary, though it doesn't itself restore control.|Stop insisting it should obey. Look for real help.|He sounds frightened by what he thought he understood.|The people of Hoenn shouldn't have had to become the lesson.|The grand ambition has encountered the consequences omitted from its own script.|A sobering moment, with an entire region beyond his voice.|We need an effective response, not only a repeated command.|A power admired from afar can become a very different thing when it moves.|His fear matters, but so do the people who never agreed to this.|I'd remember the moment his language changed from wanting more to begging it to stop.''')
add('maxie_aftermath','SootopolisCity_Text_AfterAllOurScheming','Maxie bitterly contrasts his elaborate plans with one Pokemon\'s simple resolution.',
'''neutral~The simple ending doesn't make the harm before it imaginary.|His comparison exposes how little their elaborate effort actually controlled.|Learn from it. Don't turn relief into another excuse.|That laugh sounds more unsettled than happy.|The people who lived through it need care beyond his realization.|A complicated plot has been resolved outside the ambitions that created it.|A very unkind joke played on his theory, not on the people endangered by it.|He should examine the assumptions rather than only admire the contrast in effort.|A quiet result can leave a loud responsibility behind.|The ending looks simple because someone else did what their plans couldn't.|I'd listen for whether the realization changes what he chooses afterward.''')
add('archie_pleading','SootopolisCity_Text_KyogreCalmDown','Archie cannot get Kyogre to respond to the Red Orb.',
'''neutral~The object is in his hand, but the control never was.|The failed response contradicts the assumption driving his plan.|Stop relying on what isn't working. Find another way to help.|He sounds shocked that the familiar command has no meaning here.|Everyone around him needs more than another desperate attempt.|The central prop has failed to guarantee the promised ending.|A very clear limit on the power he thought possession gave him.|Use the observed failure to revise the model, not repeat it louder.|A life cannot always be reached through the thing we think should speak for it.|His certainty has fallen away. Practical responsibility still remains.|I'd remember how long he looked at the Orb before admitting the Pokemon wasn't responding.''')
add('archie_aftermath','SootopolisCity_Text_TryingMeaninglessToPokemon','Archie reflects that their grand plans may have meant little to the ancient Pokemon.',
'''neutral~Their plans may have been small to the Pokemon. The danger wasn't small to people.|A difference in scale doesn't reduce the consequences of the choices made.|Then respect the limits. Start making things right.|It must feel strange having the whole purpose collapse into that thought.|The people affected still need care even if the ambition feels foolish now.|A grand narrator has discovered he was not directing the central characters.|A humbling thought that shouldn't become a way to dismiss the harm.|He can learn from the mismatch between intention, power, and outcome.|A small ambition can still cast a very large shadow.|The insight matters if it changes his next ordinary choice.|I'd want to hear what he is willing to do differently once the laughter stops.''')
